From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapi: Speak parses the XML markup of SAPI

sapi: Speak parses the XML markup of SAPI

ISpVoice::Speak (and SpeakStream, and ISpeechVoice) refused SPF_IS_XML,
SPF_PERSIST_XML and SPF_PARSE_SAPI with E_NOTIMPL ("flags not implemented").
They give the engine a list of text fragments now (new speak_text.c):

- volume (level, absvolume; kept within 0 to 100), rate (speed adds,
  absspeed replaces), pitch (middle and range add, absmiddle and absrange
  replace), emph, spell, pron (sym), lang (langid), context (id) and
  partofsp (part) set the state of the fragments for their content, and
  the state is restored at the closing tag; self closing tags set it for the
  rest of the enclosing element.
- silence (msec) and bookmark (mark) are fragments of their own, with the
  actions SPVA_Silence and SPVA_Bookmark; a tag that is not SAPI's goes to
  the engine as an SPVA_ParseUnknownTag fragment holding the tag text.
- Character references (the five named ones and numeric ones) are decoded,
  tag and attribute names are not case sensitive, and every text fragment
  knows its offset in the source text.
- Malformed markup (unclosed or stray tags, attributes without a quoted
  value, an unfinished tag) is SPERR_XML_BAD_SYNTAX and the engine is not
  called. SSML (SPF_PARSE_SSML) is still E_NOTIMPL, the voice tag does not
  change the voice mid text, and without the XML flags the text is spoken
  as it is, tags included, as before.

---
